{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## Final evidence pass — no code change warranted\n\nRetested the ticket's title hypothesis as a hypothesis, not a premise.\n\n### Mechanism\n- Read-only reconstruction of `origin/tickets` found **1,616** CREATE events whose title starts `Condense comments in `, all `ticket_type=task`, authored locally by `RebarBotNava`/`Rebar Bot` (`joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com`), not by `rebar-bridge[bot]`.\n- Hour distribution: `2026-09-04T20:00Z=54`, `21:00Z=183`, `22:00Z=948`, `23:00Z=314`, `2026-09-05T01:00Z=114`, then 3 stragglers at 14:00/16:00/17:00Z.\n- Dominant parent was `d8a3-ff71-8112-4e55`, epic **\"Remediate bloated source comments\"**, with **1,499** direct Condense children. Its own comment records `1,499 affected` files and `1,499 direct child tickets, one per affected file`, with validation of unique target paths and matching file impact.\n- Representative child event `77e8-b782-cd8b-462f` was `Condense comments in src/rebar/_deprecations.py`, with file impact exactly `src/rebar/_deprecations.py`; representative mid-burst child `247e-7729-fe70-414e` was `Condense comments in tests/unit/test_max_tokens_model_ceiling_1019.py`, with file impact exactly that path.\n\n### Reconciler / duplicate side\n- Related bug `00c1-dc03-1f1f-4ffc` supplied the missing experiment: `tests/integration/rebar_reconciler/test_echo_loop_experiment.py` covers binding loss, `rebar-id:` label loss, both, create-then-crash orphan, and DC index lag. Targeted run in fresh worktree: `8 passed in 17.39s`.\n- The duplicate producer was the Tier-2 eval harness live-store leak, not the reconciler. That leak is already fixed on `origin/main` via the linked-worktree `force_new_store` refusal / standalone scratch checkout path; the preventive create-surge metric is already present in `84e94070c819934e053f8883b4719cd215b14d7d` (`Add creation surge metrics`, ticket `dbe7-d957-e5da-49dd`).\n\n### Preventive control\n- Existing `create_volume_peak_hour` catches this exact incident on the real ticket-store snapshot: incident window `2026-09-04T19:00:00+00:00..2026-09-05T02:00:00+00:00` returns `{'peak_hour': 1010, 'alarm_threshold': 50, 'alarm': True}`.\n- Existing `duplicate_title_peak_hour` correctly stays false for the Condense epic because these are distinct one-file tasks with distinct file impact: same window returns `{'peak_hour': 0, 'alarm_threshold': 10, 'alarm': False}`.\n- Targeted metric test run: `python -m pytest tests/unit/metrics/test_event_metrics.py -p no:randomly -q` -> `8 passed in 4.62s`.\n\n### AC status\n- AC (a) MET: ticket comment already records operator confirmation that the Condense tickets were expected work under an in-progress epic; store evidence matches that intended epic and per-file child structure.\n- AC (b) MET: duplicate remediation comments record the duplicate population drained and related bug `00c1-dc03-1f1f-4ffc` closed after experiment.\n- AC (c) MET: `gh api repos/navapbc/rebar/actions/workflows/reconcile-bridge.yml` reports workflow state `active`.\n\nConclusion: the title conclusion survives testing for Event A. The count is **1,616** current `Condense comments in ...` tickets, not ~1,700. No new code change is warranted; the ticket should close as `not_a_bug` with this evidence."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1789925609825151169,"uuid":"56a5f168-e9ab-49a0-b49e-6e29a55eb526"}